  "notes": "Drawn from 747-8Fs N857GT (2024) and N858GT (2025). The fin is plain yellow (no DHL on it). Polar's two 777Fs (N702GT, N703GT) fly in a white and blue 'CARGO' scheme: PAC/cargo-777f. Re-checked 2026-11-15: 'Polar' lowercase measured at 0.71 of the capital P on N857GT (2024-10-01); title places and lengths agree with the photos. The yellow aft fuselage's forward edge is a straight diagonal: its points along it replaced by the two ends (2026-11-15).",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). Polar wears this co-brand on its 747-8Fs; it replaced Polar's own scheme (PAC/polar-classic) after DHL took a 49% stake (announced October 2006), on most 747-400Fs by the early 2010s. The Atlas Air and DHL joint venture ended in 2025, when Atlas Air took the rest of Polar (Wikipedia); no repaint away from the co-brand is documented yet."
